<dt>Analysis Name and Accession</dt>
<dd>
<b>Analysis Name</b>: Genome-Wide Association Meta-Analysis Of COPD From The International COPD Genetics Consortium (ICGC) And The UK Biobank<br/>
<b>Analysis Accession</b>: pha004766.1 <br/>
<b>Phenotype</b>: Pulmonary Disease, Chronic Obstructive <br/>
<b>Population</b>: European, African American, Hispanic, East Asian <br/>

<p>

	<a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genome/gdv/gwas/4766/">
	View association results in Genome Browser
	</a>
	</p>

</dd>


<dt>Analysis Description</dt>
<dd>Genome-wide association meta-analysis; included the COPDGene study, the UK Biobank, and the following ICGC cohorts: ARIC - Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, Cardiovascular Health Study (African and European ancestries), ECLIPSE - Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points, EOCOPD and ICGN - Boston Early-Onset COPD Study and International COPD Genetics Network, Lung Expression Quantitative Trait Loci Study, Framingham Heart Study, KARE - Korean Association Resource project, Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study, Korea, Lifelines, Lovelace, MESA - Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis (African, European, and Hispanic ancestries), NETT/NAS - National Emphysema Treatment Trial / Normative Aging Study, GenKOLS - Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort, Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study, Poland, Rotterdam Study (1, 2 and 3), and SPIROMICS - Subpopulations and intermediate outcome measures in COPD study.</dd>

<dt>Analysis Methods</dt>
<dd>Logistic regression, with COPD as outcome, was performed in individual cohorts, checked for orientation and hg19 chr and positions. Summary statistics for each cohort were further assessed using EasyQC. Then, a fixed-effects meta-analysis was performed using METAL. Variants from the meta-analysis were only further examined if they were present in the UK Biobank as well as at least 11 ICGC studies.</dd>





